# TypoScript setup for contexts extension Site Set
# This file is automatically included when the Site Set is activated

# Context debugging output, gated by the site setting.
#
# Deliberately a value-level `if`, not a TypoScript condition — but not because
# conditions cannot read constants. They can: IncludeTreeSetupConditionConstant-
# SubstitutionVisitor replaces {$constant} before the ExpressionLanguage ever
# sees the expression, and `[{$contexts.debug} == 1]` works once the setting
# resolves to a scalar.
#
# The reason is what happens when it does NOT. A constant with no scalar value
# is substituted with the empty string, and the condition becomes `[ == 1]` — a
# syntax error. The include tree is walked per request, so that error is logged
# twice on every single hit, in the backend as well as the frontend, and the
# gated output is unreachable regardless of the setting. That is not a
# hypothetical: it is what this extension shipped, because the settings
# definitions lived under the wrong file name (see settings.definitions.yaml).
#
# A value-level `if` fails quietly in the same situation instead of flooding the
# log. Both states are covered by Tests/Functional/SiteSetTypoScriptTest.php.
page.headerData.1700000001 = TEXT
page.headerData.1700000001 {
    value = <!-- Contexts Extension Debug Mode Active -->
    if.isTrue = {$contexts.debug}
}
